Patch 0089: recompiler CLI, progress and exit codes, deterministic output, shared resume targets taken from a frozen list.
What: ps2_recomp gets `--out`, `--elf`, `--dump-resume-owners <file>`, "[progress] done/total" lines, documented exit codes
(0 ok, 2 bad input, 3 I/O error, 4 internal; ps2xRecomp/include/ps2recomp/recompiler_exit.h), and a fixed write order, so
two runs write identical trees. A resume target claimed by several owners used to be registered by whichever owner the
unordered_map visited first. Now the function table emitter takes the owner from `general.resume_owners` (config/recomp/
resume_owners.csv, `target_address,owner_address`); a shared target missing from the list is an error naming its address
(exit 4), never a fallback to map order, and an owner that is not a candidate of its target is an error too.
`--dump-resume-owners` writes `target,owner,owner...` for every shared target (and does not fail on unlisted ones);
tools/pipeline/freeze_recomp_config.py --resume-owners-from <dump> --generated <tree> turns that into the csv.
Decision (orchestrator, T-613): resolving shared targets by a containment rule changed 1084 table entries and the game's
state from blank 240; the game as it plays today is the requirement, so today's owners are frozen. The csv holds 2059
targets taken from the register_functions.cpp that the game is built from.
Tests: ps2xTest "shared resume target goes to its frozen owner and an unlisted one fails" (listed target to its listed
owner, unlisted shared target throws with its address, collect mode lists the candidates).
Verified: ps2x_tests 432 pass, 10 fail (the known failures). Two regenerations from config/recomp.toml are identical
(diff -r empty) and equal the generated/ tree the game is built from (diff -rq empty, excluding iop_native,
sources.txt, sources_big.txt). A csv cut to 4 rows makes ps2_recomp exit 4 with "Shared resume target 0x10e63c ...".
Origin: original to this project.
